      "stageRecord": "Build both clauses using the GB categories NP, VP, IP, and CP. Subjects are generated in Spec-IP in this analysis; no VP-internal subject movement is assumed. Bought takes What as its NP complement and assigns it the Theme role, while Mary receives the Agent role. Embedded past I licenses nominative Case on Mary, and bought governs its object and assigns accusative Case to What. Say selects the declarative CP headed by overt that: John receives the Agent role and the CP receives the propositional Content role. Matrix I licenses nominative Case on John. The interrogative C is initially a separate syntactic object. Adopt a base-insertion treatment of do-support: finite did occupies matrix I as the tense carrier required for the interrogative derivation, leaving say in its bare form. This is not an analysis in which lexical say raises to C. Embedded bought is an already inflected lexical terminal licensed by abstract past I; no separate pronounced tense affix or V-to-I movement is posited. What is therefore an argument of bought, not an additional object of say.",
